  "description": "Defines the safety threshold for vehicle operations based on multiple safety factors.",
  "definition": "A vehicle is considered 'Safe for Operation' when it maintains a VPC > 0.6, has brake fluid levels above 50%, brake pad wear below 70%, adequate tire pressure (tiremetrics.pressure_kpa > 200), and is operated within recommended load limits (vehicleloadkg within manufacturer specifications)."
